A||||6||maryjane||runninhot||||1||
Z||000000||maryjane||04-26-2001||01:28 AM||||my 84 Fiero started running hot about a year ago. When I say hot, I'm used to an engine running about 180 deg in the summertime when everything is right. This one suddenly went up to 260 and pretty much stayed there till I changed the thermostat. (What is the normal temp for a 4 cyl w/ac to run on the highway?)<BR>At a light in town, it will get a little higher. I had a 1/8th hole drilled in the thermostat face and it helps a LOT, but still not right. It is not losing coolant, Just temp high. About 3 months the temp started going up and then immediatly down to around 185. This happens constantly now and sitting at a light I have to shift to neutral and give it a little gas then the temp goes back down. I've changed the water pump, belt, had rad cleaned. It is less noticeable on the highway but gauge still cycles rapidly up and down. I've noticed no combustion gas in the coolant but have not had it checked by mechanic shop. Also the engine will not start after a drive unless it cools of 30-35 minutes. It will crank over fine but won't start,unless, I pour a<BR>little gas in the throttle body. A little like what we used to call vapor lock. Once I pour gas in, it runs fine & keeps running. Any thoughts?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||04-26-2001||11:27 AM||||As far as high temps go, if it comes way up in stop and go traffic, temperature is going to be controlled more by the radiator fan than the thermostat, since it's going to be wide open. You can get lower temperature fan switches from the Fiero Store, and some other places. Stock fan switch comes on at like, 220 or something, and goes off about 180-190. Or you can flip on the A/C since that engages the fan too. As for the part about revving the motor to get it to cool down, I don't know if that's inherant in Fieros or not, but I know my old 4 banger used to do the same thing. I can only assume that considering the size of the cooling system, with all the plumbing and stuff, that at idle, the water pump just doesn't move enough water to keep things cooled off. Revving it of course will cause it to flow more. <BR>The starting thing, that's a mystery, and I don't even have a guess, unless there's a sensor someplace that's hosed. Check for codes maybe.<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||04-26-2001||02:44 PM||||My experience with the temp gage cycling up and down is proof that the thermostat is in working order. As the coolant around the motors water jacket heats up, the temp gage goes up.<BR> When it gets hot enough the thermostat opens allowing cooler coolant to enter the water jacket which cools the engine and then the temp gage goes down.<BR> This happens constantly hence the up & down on your gage.<BR> On my '84 I replaced (previous owner tore it off on a ditch) the lower front air scoop and noticed a 10-20 degree drop in temp while the car is moving, if yours is gone GM still sells them I paid about $35.00 as I recall(not installed).<BR> You didn't say if your electric coolant fan on the radiator works. If it does you should hear it run when it kicks in, if you have not heard it for a while get it checked. good luck ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||04-26-2001||04:20 PM||||Acutally, the temp should stay pretty close to the thermostats rated temp if that was controlling the temperature.  If you're getting the large temp swings (like I get on mine) it's being controlled by the fan and the thermostat is staying wide open the entire time.  Mine runs up to about 235, the fan kicks on, and it comes right back down to about 200.  Just like the factory designed.  Too hot for my tastes, but normal. I'll  probably switch to a 180* thermo and Rodney's low temp fan switch for the summer.  I don't want to go with 160* with the stock ECM, and I've heard replacing the ECM chip with a Hypertech, etc. is pretty useless.||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||04-26-2001||10:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>My experience with the temp gage cycling up and down is proof that the thermostat is in working order. As the coolant around the motors water jacket heats up, the temp gage goes up.<BR> When it gets hot enough the thermostat opens allowing cooler coolant to enter the water jacket which cools the engine and then the temp gage goes down.<BR> This happens constantly hence the up & down on your gage.<BR> On my '84 I replaced (previous owner tore it off on a ditch) the lower front air scoop and noticed a 10-20 degree drop in temp while the car is moving, if yours is gone GM still sells them I paid about $35.00 as I recall(not installed).<BR> You didn't say if your electric coolant fan on the radiator works. If it does you should hear it run when it kicks in, if you have not heard it for a while get it checked. good luck </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>cooling fan works, but only on low speed<BR>Cooling fan works but only on low speed(2 spd fan} front scoop is there but just barely.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||fierohoho||04-27-2001||11:57 PM||||As I recall, the low speed is for the engine fan switch and high is for when the A/C is on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Spektyr||04-28-2001||01:09 AM||||I've had the 160 thermostat and 176 fan switch on my 85GT for a few days now and it seems to do just fine.<P>Sure, I'm probably running richer at the lower temp, which means additional deposits, but with the way I like to rev her (well, she likes it too) I probably burn the deposits off just as fast as I put them on.<P>I figure if I keep a close eye on my plugs I'll do ok, and the hypertech chip should help to lean out the mixture to a more normal setting for the temperature.<P>I don't mind the extra work, it's a sports car.  If I want brain-dead, starts every time, never need to think about the motor kind of driving, I'll fire up the gas guzzling Lincoln.  It's got piles of hp and torque, but you'd never know it in the 40 ton body...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
